userStories.description:
**Goal** — Extract the slash transcript sink unchanged so subsequent chat wiring fits within ChatApp's source limit.

**Motivation** — While the agent runs long work the transcript only says that something is running.

**Approach** — Pure move, no behaviour change: `SlashSink` and `slashSink(title, append)` move from `ChatApp.tsx` to new `slash-sink.ts` and are exported from there. `ChatApp.tsx` imports them. This frees room under the 600-line source convention for US-003, US-005, US-006 and US-007. Verification note: `check:file-sizes` scans only `.ts` files, so the implementer confirms by line count that `ChatApp.tsx` stays under 600 lines.

Import the exported `SlashSink` type into ChatApp only if a real type annotation needs it; the moved function's return annotation consumes that type in the new module.

`slashSink` is file-local to `ChatApp.tsx` and no test imports it; UI tests reach it only through rendered output, which does not change. Retain the immediate notice path for an undefined title, buffered newline-preserving listing path for a defined title, and empty flush behavior. Add the specified sink unit tests and keep mounted /help and unknown-command output unchanged.

**Scope** — In: extraction, exports/imports and unchanged transcript behavior. Out: jobs/task footer (US-003), jobs model (US-004), /jobs behavior and output selection (US-005), stop and openers (US-006/US-007). The `check:file-sizes` baseline is not edited by any story.

**Interface** — Move this existing implementation unchanged, adding exports in `slash-sink.ts`:
```typescript
interface SlashSink {
  show(text: string): void;
  flush(): void;
}

function slashSink(title: string | undefined, append: (entry: TranscriptEntry) => void): SlashSink {
  const rows: string[] = [];
  return {
    show(text) {
      if (title === undefined) {
        append({ kind: "notice", text });
        return;
      }
      rows.push(text);
    },
    flush() {
      if (title === undefined || rows.length === 0) return;
      append({ kind: "listing", title, text: rows.join("\n") });
    },
  };
}
```
